Additional context (if relevant)": "Studies span multiple regions (Asia, Africa, Latin America) and intervention types 
(peer education, VCT, empowerment, microenterprise, structural, clinical counseling, female condom provision). Key 
findings show consistent improvements in condom use and reductions in STI/HIV incidence across diverse settings. Notable
studies include: Sonagachi empowerment model (Studies 9,11) with 25-39% increases in consistent condom use; VCT in China
(Study 7) showing OR=2.23 for condom use and OR=0.44 for STIs; brief behavioral intervention in Mexico (Study 8) with 
40% decline in STI incidence and zero HIV infections in intervention group; female condom provision in Thailand (Study 
3) reducing unprotected sex by 17%; Madagascar RCT (Study 2) showing OR=0.7 for aggregate STI with clinic-based 
counseling; and structural interventions in Nicaraguan motels (Study 67) demonstrating that environmental strategies 
(condoms in rooms) were more effective than educational materials alone."}
